# Optional overrides — zoom-mcp has no required env vars.
# Authentication is per-request via three request headers (Zoom's
# Server-to-Server OAuth app credentials — the "account_credentials" grant,
# a fully backend two-legged OAuth flow with no user redirect):
#   X-Zoom-Account-Id — the S2S OAuth app's Account ID
#   X-Zoom-Client-Id — the S2S OAuth app's Client ID
#   X-Zoom-Client-Secret — the S2S OAuth app's Client Secret
#
# This server performs a fresh OAuth token exchange on every single tool
# call:
#   POST https://zoom.us/oauth/token?grant_type=account_credentials&account_id=...
#     Authorization: Basic base64(client_id:client_secret)
#   -> {"access_token": "...", "expires_in": 3599, ...}
# The access_token (valid only 1 hour, no refresh token) is then sent as
# "Authorization: Bearer <token>" on the real API call. Nothing is cached
# or persisted across MCP calls.

MCP_HTTP_PORT=8080
MCP_HTTP_HOST=0.0.0.0
